                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "76a6513b-c6ef-39ed-834c-57b55202f0f3",
                        "entry_id": "3d0370ff-2373-342b-925c-f6452d3c20c5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An act of jeering or heckling."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "63fabe49-19fa-4c2f-85b6-fa5ac64e5295",
                                "sense_id": "76a6513b-c6ef-39ed-834c-57b55202f0f3",
                                "text": "It's the sort of mindset in which you don't take in the words of praise, only the boss's criticism and the barrackings of the crowd."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d0516bd1-ffe0-30d1-a1b9-eb03292b5481",
                        "entry_id": "3d0370ff-2373-342b-925c-f6452d3c20c5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The act of cheering for or supporting a team."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "New-Zealand"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7acdfc32-8c71-465c-aca5-36cb818cc89f",
                                "sense_id": "d0516bd1-ffe0-30d1-a1b9-eb03292b5481",
                                "text": "The only really unique aspect of Australian barracking is its idiom, the distinctive language and humour involved."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc3353ea-a962-4be0-ab95-7c3af9088ea6",
                                "sense_id": "d0516bd1-ffe0-30d1-a1b9-eb03292b5481",
                                "text": "I had by then explained to him my custom of occasionally listening to Australian Rules Football on our shortwave radio of a Saturday afternoon; how, despite my barracking for Essendon, I thought a player from Geelong, Gary Ablett, the best I had ever seen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "76bd652b-297f-459e-a4f9-1bcd9e977dea",
                                "sense_id": "d0516bd1-ffe0-30d1-a1b9-eb03292b5481",
                                "text": "‘So to me barracking for the footy I identified with my father, although nobody barracked for Essendon.’"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
